    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0774" n="652" xml:id="pg652"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Loring.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 10,
                        1889</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department was glad to receive your No.
                    7, of the 9th ultimo, touching the remission of the fine imposed on Captain
                    Colcord, of the American bark <hi rendition="#italic">Carrie Heckle</hi>, at
                    Lourenço Marques.</p>
                <p>In view of a letter from Messrs. A. Mudgett &amp; Co., of 39 South street, New
                    York, dated the 5th instant, I have to ask that you will kindly collect the
                    amount and remit the same to the above company through this Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
